# `@ ((F, !go))` in a plain function, outside any tag's arm: a bundle with a function
# part as a blueprint's output, applied by a block's line that binds its parts (Type
# System ch. 2: `@ x` is the blueprint whose output is `x`; a function is a value, and a
# plain aggregate with a functor value inside is a bundle; Semantics ch. 8: a blueprint
# builds nothing until a block applies it). Written by Claude on the claude-lowering
# branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

?Made: fn (fn Nat -> Nat), !Click -> ?@((fn Nat -> Nat, !Click))
fn ?Made F, !go = ? @ ((F, !go))

@page: @unit
@page:
    !go <- Ui.Button($label=$"go")
    match ?Made (\|n| n + 1), !go:
        ? @t:
            ((F, !again)) <- @t
            $count <- 0 then $count + 1 on !again
            Ui.Label($text=$"{F 5} {$count}")
        nil: Ui.Label($text=$"none")
